.TH ISI 1 "November 2026" "isi 1.0.2" "isi manual"
.SH NAME
isi \- text editor for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isi
.RB [ \-r ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isi
is a text editor for the terminal. It fills the whole window inside a
frame, with the menus at the top and the text below. Menus open with the
mouse, with
.B F10
or with
.B Alt
and the first letter of the menu, and are browsed with Tab or the arrow
keys.
.PP
If the file does not exist, it is created when saved. If it was
encrypted with
.BR isi ,
the password is asked for when it is opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
Open the file read\-only.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+A, Ctrl+G, Ctrl+T, Ctrl+Q
Open, save, save as and quit.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y
Undo and redo.
.TP
.B Ctrl+X, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V
Cut, copy and paste. Copied text is also sent to the terminal
(OSC 52) and, if they exist, to
.BR wl\-copy ,
.B xclip
or
.BR xsel .
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V
Paste what was copied outside isi (a web page, a document). This is the
terminal's own paste and needs nothing installed.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Select all.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D, Ctrl+B
Duplicate and delete the line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Remove the empty lines of the selection or, with no selection, of the
whole text.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F, F3, Shift+F3
Search, next and previous. The search is not case sensitive.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Search and replace.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Go to a line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Show or hide line numbers.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Defang the IOCs of the text or of the selection.
.TP
.B Home, End
Start and end of the text. With
.B Alt
held, start and end of the line.
.TP
.B Shift+arrows
Select. Text can also be selected by dragging with the mouse, and a
double click selects a word.
.TP
.B Ctrl+H, F1
List of shortcuts.
.SH TABLES
The
.B Table
menu inserts tables in Markdown or box style, with the chosen number of
columns and rows. Inside a table,
.B Tab
and
.B Shift+Tab
move from cell to cell and
.B Enter
goes down to the first cell of the next row, creating it if it is the
last one. Columns widen by themselves while typing.
.SH CSV
.B .csv
and
.B .tsv
files open as a sheet: aligned columns, fixed header row and cell by
cell editing.
.B File \(-> Open CSV
opens any other file this way. On saving, only the edited cells change;
the separator, the quotes and the line breaks are kept.
.TP
.B Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter
Next cell, previous cell and row below. On the last row they create a
new one.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D, Ctrl+B
Duplicate and delete the row.
.TP
.B Alt+\(da
Column menu: sort from A to Z or from Z to A and filter. Also with a
click on the arrow of the header.
.PP
Sorting recognises numbers, IP addresses and dates (ISO 8601 and
dd/mm/yyyy); text is sorted ignoring case and accents, and empty cells
go last.
.PP
The filter shows the values of the column with how many times each one
appears, sortable by frequency, and accepts expressions:
.I text
(contains),
.B * ?
(wildcards),
.B 192.168.1.0/24
(network),
.BR > ,
.BR >= ,
.BR < ,
.BR <= ,
.B =
(comparison),
.B a..b
(range),
.B !
(negation) and
.B |
(or). Several columns can be filtered at once.
.PP
.B File \(-> Convert CSV to table
creates a Markdown or box table with the visible rows. With no CSV open
it asks for the file, detects the separator and converts Latin\-1 files
to UTF\-8.
.SH IOC
The
.B IOCs
menu highlights domains, IP addresses, URLs, executable names and MD5,
SHA\-1 and SHA\-256 hashes, also inside code.
.B Defang IOCs
(Ctrl+W) turns them into a form that cannot be clicked or opened by
mistake, such as
.BR evil[.]com ,
.B 1[.]2[.]3[.]4
or
.BR hxxp:// ,
and
.B Refang IOCs
does the opposite. With
.B Defang while typing
they are defanged as soon as they are typed or pasted.
.B Copy IOC list
copies every indicator to the clipboard, without repetitions.
.SH ENCRYPTION
.B File \(-> Encrypt
asks for a password of at least 15 characters with letters, numbers and
symbols. From then on the file is saved encrypted with
XChaCha20\-Poly1305. The key is derived from the password with Argon2id
(64 MiB of memory, 3 passes). If the password is lost, there is no way to
recover the content.
.PP
.B File \(-> Remove encryption
saves it in clear again.
.SH LANGUAGE
The interface is available in 23 languages. The first time, the system
language is used (variables
.BR LANGUAGE ,
.BR LC_ALL ,
.B LC_MESSAGES
and
.BR LANG )
if it is available, and Spanish otherwise.
.B View \(-> Language
changes it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/isi/config
Language and preferences (line numbers and IOC options). If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set, that directory is used.
.TP
.IB file ~
Rescue copy written if the terminal is closed or the program receives
SIGHUP or SIGTERM with unsaved changes. If the file was encrypted, the
copy is encrypted too.
.SH LIMITS
Files larger than 1 GB are not opened.
.SH MESSAGES
Messages appear in a row at the bottom, which closes by itself after a
minute, with a double click or with
.BR Esc .
.SH SECURITY
Control characters and escape sequences in the file are shown as
.B ^X
and are never sent to the terminal. Invisible and text direction
characters are shown as
.BR ? .
Saving first writes a temporary file and then renames it, so an
interruption halfway does not leave a half\-written file.
